[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439393853","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98542#issuecomment-2439393853","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98542","id":2439393853,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RZjI9","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-26T06:38:58Z","updated_at":"2024-10-26T06:38:58Z","body":"I think this is expected. It's no different from:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends Node\r\n\r\nvar sprite: Sprite2D\r\n\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n\tsprite.foo = 42\r\n```\r\n\r\nSomeone could extend `Sprite2D` and add a `foo` to it.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439393853/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439394597","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98542#issuecomment-2439394597","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98542","id":2439394597,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RZjUl","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-26T06:40:38Z","updated_at":"2024-10-26T06:45:50Z","body":"> I think this is expected. It's no different from:\r\n> \r\n> ```gdscript\r\n> extends Node\r\n> \r\n> var sprite: Sprite2D\r\n> \r\n> func _ready() -> void:\r\n> \tsprite.foo = 42\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> Someone could extend `Sprite2D` and add a `foo` to it.\r\n\r\nHowever, this would result in a error during the runtime if `foo` does not exist in that class. I tested this.\r\nBesides, there is no any extra documentation that says that you are allowed to add a new member *dynamically* by such an operation.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439394597/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439425101","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98542#issuecomment-2439425101","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98542","id":2439425101,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RZqxN","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-26T08:06:23Z","updated_at":"2024-10-26T08:06:23Z","body":"This is not a bug. I remember there was a similar issue/discussion about the `self.` prefix. GDScript is strict only when you use pure identifiers. If you use complex expressions like property access (`some_expression.property`), GDScript assumes that you may want dynamic access.\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nself.lalala # OK\r\nlalala # Compile-time error `Identifier \"lalala\" not declared in the current scope.`\r\n```\r\n\r\nGDScript is not a strictly statically typed language, so if something is possible at runtime, it should not produce a compile-time error, at most an `UNSAFE_*` warning (disabled by default). For example, a property can be declared in a derived class (subtype) or implemented dynamically using `_set()` and `_get()`.\r\n\r\nIf you want GDScript to produce warnings or errors for non-existent properties (as if GDScript were a statically typed language), you can change the appropriate project settings. See [Static typing in GDScript - Warning system](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/static_typing.html#warning-system).\r\n\r\n![](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/23743355-5a0b-4791-9ef7-55647eba2f58)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2439425101/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]